---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/pages/the-method.css';
---

<Layout title="The Method: Secure Prospective" description="Diagnose, Position, Shape, Transform, and Re-diagnose inside the operating business first.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="method-page" transition:name="page-card">
    <section class="method-hero" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="method-hero-grid shell">
        <div class="method-hero-index">
          <span>FILE // METHOD</span>
          <span>CYCLE // OPEN</span>
          <div class="method-index-note" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="method-index-mark"></span>
            <span>APPLIED<br />IN ORDER</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="method-hero-main">
          <div class="method-hero-copy">
            <h1 id="method-title">The method goes to work here first.</h1>
            <p>
              Diagnose, Position, Shape, and Transform are not four boxes on a consulting slide. They are
              controls applied to the business that already has to perform.
            </p>
          </div>

          <nav class="method-loop" aria-label="Method sequence">
            <div class="method-loop-header">
              <span>CONTROL LOOP</span>
              <span data-cycle-status>01 // DIAGNOSE</span>
            </div>
            <ol class="method-loop-list">
              <li class="is-current">
                <a class="method-loop-link" href="#diagnose" data-cycle-link="0" aria-current="step">
                  <span class="method-loop-number">01</span>
                  <span class="method-loop-name"><strong>Diagnose</strong><small>Constraint first</small></span>
                  <span class="method-loop-state">INPUT</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a class="method-loop-link" href="#position" data-cycle-link="1">
                  <span class="method-loop-number">02</span>
                  <span class="method-loop-name"><strong>Position</strong><small>Place capability</small></span>
                  <span class="method-loop-state">BOUNDARY</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a class="method-loop-link" href="#shape" data-cycle-link="2">
                  <span class="method-loop-number">03</span>
                  <span class="method-loop-name"><strong>Shape</strong><small>Make output ownable</small></span>
                  <span class="method-loop-state">OUTPUT</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a class="method-loop-link" href="#transform" data-cycle-link="3">
                  <span class="method-loop-number">04</span>
                  <span class="method-loop-name"><strong>Transform</strong><small>Change the operation</small></span>
                  <span class="method-loop-state">EVIDENCE</span>
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a class="method-loop-link" href="#re-diagnose" data-cycle-link="4">
                  <span class="method-loop-number">05</span>
                  <span class="method-loop-name"><strong>Re-diagnose</strong><small>Secure the next state</small></span>
                  <span class="method-loop-state">RETURN</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            </ol>
            <div class="method-loop-return" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="method-loop-return-line"></span>
              <strong>05 RETURNS TO 01</strong>
            </div>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="method-cycle-heading" aria-labelledby="cycle-title">
      <div class="method-cycle-heading-grid shell">
        <div class="method-cycle-heading-index">
          <span>METHOD // APPLIED</span>
          <span>READ // IN ORDER</span>
        </div>
        <div class="method-cycle-heading-copy">
          <h2 id="cycle-title">Not four boxes. A working cycle.</h2>
          <p>
            The controls are applied to the business that already has to perform. Each movement changes the
            conditions for the next.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ol class="method-stations" aria-label="Five movements of the operating method">
      <li id="diagnose" class="method-station method-station--diagnose is-current" data-cycle-station="0" data-cycle-name="DIAGNOSE">
        <article class="method-station-grid shell" aria-labelledby="diagnose-title">
          <div class="method-station-rail">
            <span class="method-station-code">CONTROL 01</span>
            <span class="method-station-number">01</span>
            <strong>Diagnose</strong>
            <span class="method-station-state">CONSTRAINT FIRST</span>
            <span class="method-station-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="method-station-body">
            <h3 id="diagnose-title">Find the constraint before the tool.</h3>
            <p class="method-station-copy">
              The IMO is metered as an operating system: people, cases, decisions, handoffs, data, delay, and
              responsibility. Symptoms do not receive software. The root constraint receives a diagnosis.
            </p>
            <figure class="quote-field method-quote method-quote--yellow">
              <figcaption>FAILURE CONDITION // DIAGNOSE</figcaption>
              <blockquote>A wrong diagnosis makes every correct build irrelevant.</blockquote>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>

      <li id="position" class="method-station method-station--position" data-cycle-station="1" data-cycle-name="POSITION">
        <article class="method-station-grid shell" aria-labelledby="position-title">
          <div class="method-station-rail">
            <span class="method-station-code">CONTROL 02</span>
            <span class="method-station-number">02</span>
            <strong>Position</strong>
            <span class="method-station-state">BOUNDARY FIRST</span>
            <span class="method-station-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="method-station-body">
            <h3 id="position-title">Put capability where consequences are understood.</h3>
            <p class="method-station-copy">
              AI placed without context creates confidence in the wrong output. Positioning defines where a
              tool belongs, what information it may use, where a human must intervene, and what cannot be delegated.
            </p>
            <ul class="method-controls" aria-label="Positioning controls">
              <li>
                <span class="method-control-letter">A</span>
                <strong>Environment</strong>
                <p>Understand the people, process, data, and obligations surrounding the tool.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="method-control-letter">B</span>
                <strong>Boundary</strong>
                <p>Name what the system may decide, assist, surface, or never touch.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="method-control-letter">C</span>
                <strong>Owner</strong>
                <p>Keep a responsible person attached to every consequential output.</p>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>

      <li id="shape" class="method-station method-station--shape" data-cycle-station="2" data-cycle-name="SHAPE">
        <article class="method-station-grid shell" aria-labelledby="shape-title">
          <div class="method-station-rail">
            <span class="method-station-code">CONTROL 03</span>
            <span class="method-station-number">03</span>
            <strong>Shape</strong>
            <span class="method-station-state">OUTPUT FIRST</span>
            <span class="method-station-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="method-station-body">
            <h3 id="shape-title">Structure output so the operation can hold it.</h3>
            <p class="method-station-copy">
              Output no one understands is output no one owns. SP+ must make work inspectable, correctable,
              and transferable. The system serves the operator. It does not become an unchallengeable black box.
            </p>
            <dl class="method-output-register" aria-label="Shape output requirements">
              <div>
                <dt>Output</dt>
                <dd>Legible</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Decision</dt>
                <dd>Traceable</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Ownership</dt>
                <dd>Human-held</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>

      <li id="transform" class="method-station method-station--transform" data-cycle-station="3" data-cycle-name="TRANSFORM">
        <article class="method-station-grid shell" aria-labelledby="transform-title">
          <div class="method-station-rail">
            <span class="method-station-code">CONTROL 04</span>
            <span class="method-station-number">04</span>
            <strong>Transform</strong>
            <span class="method-station-state">EVIDENCE FIRST</span>
            <span class="method-station-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="method-station-body">
            <h3 id="transform-title">Change the operation, not the vocabulary.</h3>
            <p class="method-station-copy">
              AI-powered means a feature was added. AI-native means the architecture of the work changed.
              Transformation is not declared when SP+ runs. It is demonstrated when the operation works differently
              because SP+ is part of it.
            </p>
            <figure class="quote-field method-quote method-quote--blue">
              <figcaption>FIELD TEST // TRANSFORM</figcaption>
              <blockquote>The deliverable must survive contact with the business.</blockquote>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>

      <li id="re-diagnose" class="method-station method-station--rediagnose" data-cycle-station="4" data-cycle-name="RE-DIAGNOSE">
        <article class="method-station-grid shell" aria-labelledby="re-diagnose-title">
          <div class="method-station-rail">
            <span class="method-station-code">CONTROL 05</span>
            <span class="method-station-number">↺</span>
            <strong>Re-diagnose</strong>
            <span class="method-station-state">NEXT STATE</span>
            <span class="method-station-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="method-station-body">
            <h3 id="re-diagnose-title">Secure the next state.</h3>
            <p class="method-station-copy">
              Every prospective system eventually becomes part of the operating foundation. Once it does, the
              work is measured again. New constraints surface. The next cycle begins without pretending the future
              has stopped moving.
            </p>
            <div class="method-return-register" aria-label="Cycle return">
              <div class="method-return-register-head">
                <span>RETURN PATH</span>
                <span>05 / 01</span>
              </div>
              <div class="method-return-track" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="method-return-track-point"></span>
                <span class="method-return-track-rule"></span>
                <span class="method-return-track-point"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="method-return-register-foot">
                <span>RE-DIAGNOSE</span>
                <span>DIAGNOSE</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a class="action action--dark" href="/the-work#sp-plus">See the active application <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/motion.js';
  import '../scripts/pages/the-method.js';
</script>
